  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Combating Transnational Threats Senior Executive Seminar 03-21: &quot;Nuclear Weapons Proliferations: Strategic Implications for the NESA Region&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Focused on &quot;Nuclear Weapons Proliferations: Strategic Implications for the NESA Region&quot;. The proliferation of nuclear weapons and their delivery systems.ballistic and cruise missiles.pose a grave threat to international security, especially in the Middle East and South Asia. This seminar will survey the status of declared and undeclared nuclear weapons arsenals around the globe. It will examine the US, Chinese, Russian, British, French nuclear weapons programs. This survey will serve as an analytic base from which to study suspected or opaque nuclear weapons programs in North Korea, Iran, Israel, Pakistan, and India. The seminar also will explore the geopolitical incentives for other states to pursue similar nuclear strategic postures and how the proliferation of nuclear weapons could impact deterrence, crisis instability, and war fighting in the Middle East and South Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
